    "notes": {
        "cd68a58d-ffe8-4c16-ba34-4d2167eeb561": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 288,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Timing\n\nThe query returns the row `id = 1` with `ts` = the current UNIX timestamp, so the row changes on every poll and UpdatedRow emits it.\n\nThe first poll after the flow starts is skipped and the start itself only records the baseline, so the trigger fires on the **second poll** after start. The AfterAll timeout (420 s) must stay longer than two tick intervals of the instance. No tables are needed."
        }
    }
